{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb173a4878095378407506e4b748e6903f73c2afb48","commits":["52c1f25597da3d5804444bf4a25fd37cba3dfd2f","841bdf6cf99fbce9add808ee8b777f67edefbf48","51821ff170cdbf530a83c87ccd5bbcdbad385609","417baa12d55980ebab0eeccd2f5ca44b3f911a59","8c70a3e52dbb5450ef704b17614e9b50b4892099","c17b2d7e48be4d8f4f31dedd4f8ed15fb6534ea8","64c1aa95340f6af8ab65ca818ff63476e35784d7","dac7228a03e87a9012f4baee2b803cb2011c3d2e","a3536a0bbc7fdc2e46cc555509e973b02afc02c4","f6f5a1c272776077a99c1e0e641b7ca9cf0a1d29","460ce4ee42ab26909e9ccaa54bd24d9488dbd280","18d0be594a67b5bf687d1d4b33ffef905ddcbbf4","d443c65267f2b586f40999cee00e826debf7e83d","8d8640be78f4ad7d396484caff44cc8f6ccbb08a","a7b5815c1d31ab3d00bc78253457213cf78a5d37","b4bb51b860b21f1871678a1a54b4842464905e9d","8aa8d24781533a385f0352d1fd37811b7f4ed075","65b1a6e09d6ad691351ca5e0ab6a96996c20567d","76bcc81ca940bc1ed6f12a2c2b1c86ac1e3465f6","a436ac2ce7c28e6f70a8e2806aa8201823b5bc6f","f992293aaea90dd9476f2e184f9c49cb35cc6e96","bfea3dbc3023e4c36f5d7df4761219b266f293bb","ba1b3793e2353fb0b64b37bd2eaf8db78ad6899b"],"user_facing":false,"packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb186e10906c90d7ad7e9a846f08da0aaee3399e985","commits":["d7d79ff5c4fe2b22862e2afdca40279d4549a3f4","a6a488193e2fad2f53487235fe1d70331c624e65","8943c6ce675c0f50769407233a125d11a107b44e","5968bbd58b8edf337a2548acea64426d9749b415"],"user_facing":false,"packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb3279f9cc6a22fecdc4fe34978be2336cc11420e8e","commits":["63970a82f01404f7dc17fa1b7266f25de46937f1","2506e5959df6c1cb0e92b4d6d4b6b7f5a1cca7ff","80d20394fd270e4d4c032973a217e00bb22bad23","26b7ef13b4abeecb8cdd083a9ed6a6e0d8959984","e4c1130f0d1d37cc18a3109e716d4ad5a99d0421"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**selfdoc is one Go binary now, and the `selfblog` command is gone.** Install it with `go install github.com/smm-h/selfdoc/cmd/selfdoc@v0`, or download the archive for your platform from the GitHub Release; every `selfblog X` invocation is now `selfdoc X`, so a post-release hook running `selfblog assembly push` must be changed to `selfdoc assembly push`.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb77e74173467064cb1e2184c06abbefdcc5a9774e2","commits":["4b268383d880c7cc5cd0646bb589e6bfef292a82","e0338f80aaa17674d98430fe9540cc5b9421b018","f4e5cad65add37dd4087c9ac0fc62c38e56f1d2b","e213e40572c85d76662ac7411db3063d3a2871db"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**One `build` builds every kind of site and one `check` checks every kind of project.** `build --target site|posts|unified|home` selects what to build, and `check` validates whichever kind of project it is pointed at, so the refusals each of the two former CLIs raised against the other kind of project are gone.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb794427fae1dd39e2f121e4d02a56ab40a452a34da","commits":["5b1df49dc02cb34759647cac07c1aeb0c0bfc951","3443759e3e68dfdc7288239a5fcd65039f55ca07"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Custom directives run out of process through `python3`.** The `resolve(attrs, config, body)` contract is unchanged, so existing scripts keep working, but a script that fails or that defines no `resolve` is now a hard error that stops the build instead of an inline note left in the page.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb7a9237bbcd592a8508eb94077ac6ce7668e19e6f1","commits":["10d42c7ae64ed6c8689e9537e631871698b92646"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Syntax highlighting comes from chroma, whose token class names differ from pygments.** Highlighted code carries chroma class names, so custom CSS written against the old pygments classes must be re-pointed; the stylesheet selfdoc generates follows the new names by itself.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb7b8e226314095c0dbd1f44e4d9b9639821c2f43ed","commits":["944a75b516a6b6be9bc21a8d105545323c86875b"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Open Graph cards are the basic generated PNG only.** Every page still gets an OG image, drawn by the built-in generator; the richer pre-drawn card path is gone.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb7c836678c23a4bdceb0b448c0b0b9e3d3f3e198d0","commits":["13b04f7efadb115c8805d7f10c879ed72b0f1af4","029125635c11bcfa8327d4f1c123a526523e8914"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The assembly deploy workflow installs the Go binary and pins one version.** The generated workflow runs `go install` instead of installing two Python packages, and `assembly sync-workflow` takes `--pin-selfdoc` and `--pin-pagefind` to choose the versions it writes; regenerate the workflow with `selfdoc assembly sync-workflow` after upgrading.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb9a7e1a083b6d72e2ec442472991ef5bd8b7e1c23f","commits":["68512d73949c734585c6fa585790f4227c636f6c","5b1df49dc02cb34759647cac07c1aeb0c0bfc951"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**`python3` is needed only for custom directives.** The build, the blog, the assembly and every language extractor -- Python included -- run inside the one binary, so a project that declares no custom directive script needs no interpreter at all.","type":"feature","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb9bdca090519a2add7e6b04d9aa52344403795195a","commits":["871d6cc86cdd0c0a92d2a20683ca74418f51341b","80d20394fd270e4d4c032973a217e00bb22bad23","d5ccf5114227597268ced1d359621ebbceedb69d"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The Python-only dependencies are gone.** Installing selfdoc no longer pulls a Python dependency set along with it: the themes, browser scripts, word list and document validators are compiled into the binary.","type":"feature","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb9d37a546fd387459f18b0494394c938cca93165ea","commits":["638c7532f2a72b71823ea4cfd793bb318221dfea"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**A Go package reads its documentation from a fixed file.** Package documentation no longer depends on which file the source walk reached first, so rebuilding a Go project's reference pages gives the same package text every time.","type":"fix","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4adb9e3a3ffaedeae597fdcf94bb693c16046da8ee825","commits":["8b21672a7445fb621b8e3e7ce8ea313c7c224021"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The check report keeps a directive's attributes in the order the template wrote them.** A directive line in `selfdoc check` output reads back the way it was written instead of in a reordered form.","type":"fix","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4b432c5b57967bfceec5c5a2c426ca40279fc45b0b023","commits":["dadccb0d10a95d6b549eb1e8fb87df70af8a1158","98b293b3c34ea3c0d9cbd839705fa074cec9c407","9c1ab5bedd1ae1a373bbc2350842f427bf6d5e77","a3644975661b3a3eedfebccb5b29a8df64084de6"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Documenting Python no longer needs a Python interpreter.** selfdoc reads Python source itself, so `gen`, `build` and `check` work on a machine with no `python3` installed -- reference pages, signatures and field tables render exactly as before.","type":"feature","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4b4481c4c8bd92f4d189de85640228d74d1a302f4e5df","commits":["1ba828800cf9a6ca84b85e4388be68680eac6f1a"],"user_facing":false,"packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4b459b0655cf26d6f5633499a49bc92f061b012d29f36","commits":["908f7367e1b68d3307516e5e296c52b65743a4fc"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Home-project pages wrap site-level directive output in `<selfdoc-region>` instead of `<selfblog-region>`.** The unified assembly refreshes only regions carrying the new tag, so redeploy the home project once after upgrading (`selfdoc blog publish-docs` from the home checkout, or its next release); until then its project cards and newest-post block stay as last published.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18d4b459c57174e05aa357a6550347a89c9c8b518a330c4a","commits":["83cba521a50fa68842f1744de00f4afd5c2b5a90"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**The editor reads its repository list from `~/Projects/ark/selfdoc-registry.toml` by default.** Move an existing `selfblog-registry.toml` to the new name, or pass `--registry` with the old path.","type":"breaking","packages":["root"]}
